# Name of benchmark/experiment: FILLET Experiment 4 (CO2 bifurcation)
# Code: AVALON (Albedo-feedback Variable Axial-tilt Latitudinal Outgoing-Net EBM)
# Describe how ice line latitude is determined: latitude where the annual-mean surface temperature crosses 0.00 C, linearly interpolated in latitude between cell centers. Land and Sea columns are identical (one temperature per band).
# Conventions: ice-free NMax=NMin=90, SMax=SMin=-90; snowball NMax=90 NMin=0 SMax=0 SMin=-90; polar cap NMax=90 NMin=edge (SMax=-edge SMin=-90); belt NMax/NMin = poleward/equatorward edges. If a cap and a belt coexist the cap is reported.
# Mode: seasonal (limit cycle; values are means over the final orbit)
# Orbital period (days): 365.0000; steps per orbit: 366 (dt = 0.9973 days; even count, so the sampled seasonal forcing is mirror-symmetric between hemispheres); grid: 90 equal-area cells in sin(lat), cell-centered, no node on the poles
# Albedo land/ocean/ice: 0.3000/0.2000/0.6000; heat capacity land/ocean/ice: 1e+07/4e+08/1e+07 J m^-2 K^-1; D = 0.5000 W m^-2 K^-1
# OLR = A + B*T - F*ln(CO2/280 ppm), T in C: A = 210.00 W m^-2, B = 2.000 W m^-2 K^-1, F = 5.35 W m^-2
# Ice: linear transition of width 1.00 K centered on 0.00 C; an ice-covered band takes the ice albedo and the ice heat capacity (from the instantaneous temperature)
# Land fraction: 0.25 uniform (FILLET Table 4); one temperature per band (land and ocean blended in albedo and heat capacity)
# Configuration: Benchmark 2 (un-tuned FILLET Table 4 parameters), obliquity 23.5
# Note: with OLR = A + B*T - F*ln(CO2/280) the CO2 forcing over 1-1e5 ppm is 62 W m^-2, less than a snowball needs to deglaciate at S = 1 (~74 W m^-2, i.e. ~3e8 ppm), so the cold-start branch stays glaciated over the whole range
# Branches: warm = warm start (uniform 30.0 C) sweeping CO2 downward; cold = cold start (uniform -50.0 C) sweeping upward. Each case starts from the final state of the previous case (continuation).
# Per-case convergence and hemispheric-symmetry diagnostics are kept with the AVALON repository (convergence.log and per-case lat files)
#
# Columns: Case = case number; Inst = instellation (S_earth = 1361 W m^-2); Obl = obliquity (deg); XCO2 = CO2 mixing ratio (ppm); Tglob = area-weighted annual mean surface temperature (K); IceLine* = ice edges (deg, see above); Diff = diffusion coefficient used (W m^-2 K^-1); OLRglob = area-weighted annual mean OLR (W m^-2); Branch = warm (warm start, decreasing sweep) or cold (cold start, increasing sweep)
# Case Inst Obl XCO2 Tglob IceLineNMaxLand IceLineNMinLand IceLineNMaxSea IceLineNMinSea IceLineSMaxLand IceLineSMinLand IceLineSMaxSea IceLineSMinSea Diff OLRglob Branch
